# README Requirements

When generating or editing `README.md`, include the following sections in this exact order.

---

## 1. Title & Description

```markdown
# yes-toto

A faithful C implementation of the Unix `yes` command.
Outputs a string (default: `y`) repeatedly and infinitely to stdout,
until killed or its output pipe is closed.
```

---

## 2. Requirements

```markdown
## Requirements

- GCC or Clang
- GNU Make
- A POSIX-compatible system (Linux, macOS, BSD)
```

---

## 3. Building

```markdown
## Building

\`\`\`bash
git clone https://github.com/youruser/yes-toto
cd yes-toto
make
\`\`\`

The binary will be placed at `./yes-toto`.

To clean build artifacts:
\`\`\`bash
make clean
\`\`\`
```

---

## 4. Usage

Must cover all behaviors from the behavioral contract in `01-project-overview`:

```markdown
## Usage

\`\`\`bash
# Print "y" forever (default)
yes-toto

# Print a custom string forever
yes-toto hello

# Print multiple arguments joined by a space
yes-toto a b c

# Use with a pipe — exits cleanly when the pipe closes
yes-toto | head -5

# Show version, author, and licence
yes-toto --version
yes-toto -v

# Show usage help
yes-toto --help
yes-toto -h
\`\`\`
```

---

